Jar:
-----
1. Packages Java classes, libraries, and resources into a single archive. Used for standalone apps or reusable libraries.
2. Extension is .jar.
3. Jar files consists of compiled .class files, resources and meta-inf/manifest.mf files.
4. Use cases-Normap spring boot apps are often packaged as jar.
5. Jar file can be directly making use of the command java -jar myApp.jar.

War:
-----
1. War file will be packaging your entire application including jsp, servlets, html, css and static resources as well.
2. Uses .war extension.
3. war will be containing all the compiled files, libraries, jsp and  etc in your web.xml in web-inf folder.


